       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Animated Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is an animated landing page?\", \"a\": \"An animated landing page is a single page with one goal, such as a signup or a demo request, that uses motion to make a point. Steps slide in on scroll, a counter climbs, or a short product loop plays. The offer still reads clearly with every animation switched off.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create an animated landing page?\", \"a\": \"List each animation with its job and its length, and keep the headline and main button still. Then describe the page to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder'>AI landing page builder</a>, which builds it from that prompt, motion included. Before you publish, load it with reduced motion turned on and send a test through every form.\"}, {\"q\": \"Does landing page animation slow down the page?\", \"a\": \"It can, depending on what you animate. web.dev notes that an animation that moves an element using something other than transform is likely to be slow. Slide elements with transform, fade them with opacity, and compress any video loop before it goes on the page.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should I look for in animated landing page examples?\", \"a\": \"Look at when each animation starts and stops, not only how it looks. Scroll each example slowly, then fast, and check that the text reads at both speeds. Then reload it with the reduce motion setting on. If a product needs a minute of motion to explain, study a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/video'>video landing page</a> instead of a long loop.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should animated landing pages play their animations automatically?\", \"a\": \"Short ones can; long ones need a control. Under WCAG 2.2.2, motion that starts automatically, lasts more than 5 seconds, and plays in parallel with other content needs a pause, stop, or hide control. A counter that finishes in 2 seconds needs nothing extra. A product loop that keeps going needs a pause button.\"}, {\"q\": \"Which landing page animation examples are worth copying?\", \"a\": \"Copy the ones that explain something. A scroll reveal suits a process in 3 steps, a counter suits a running total, and a short loop suits a product doing its main task. Skip motion that only decorates, such as a spinning logo or a headline that types itself out letter by letter.\"}, {\"q\": \"Does a landing page with animation work the same on a phone?\", \"a\": \"Not entirely. A phone has no cursor to rest on a card, and a hover effect there fires only on a tap, if at all. Trigger it on scroll or tap instead. Test on a real phone as well: a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/mobile'>mobile landing page</a> is read one screen at a time, and every animation competes for that small space.\"}, {\"q\": \"What code makes landing page animations start on scroll?\", \"a\": \"The Intersection Observer API lets the page observe when an element starts to intersect the viewport, the part of the page on screen. At that moment the page adds a class, and the element slides or fades in. Emergent writes that code from your prompt, and paid plans export it to your GitHub repository.\"}, {\"q\": \"How many animations should an animated landing page have?\", \"a\": \"As few as have a job: at most one per section, and none on the headline or the main button. If two things move on the same screen at once, cut one. Count them before you publish; on a long page, four is plenty.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can an animated landing page include a signup form with steps?\", \"a\": \"Yes. A <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/multi-step'>multi step form</a> fits an animated landing page well: each step slides in after the last answer, and a progress bar fills as the visitor goes. Emergent builds conversational flows with one question per screen, and every answer saves to a database you own.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6af709944a92a552531bb5d7",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Competitor Comparison FAQ\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What are competitor comparison landing pages?\", \"a\": \"Competitor comparison landing pages are pages on your own site that compare your product with one named rival, row by row. They answer a search for one product against the other, or for an alternative to the rival, with a table and one next step, such as a trial.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create competitor comparison landing pages?\", \"a\": \"Write down the search you want to answer, pick six to eight rows buyers decide on, and find the source for every rival claim. Then describe the page to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder'>AI landing page builder</a>. It builds the table and the form from your prompt, and each lead lands in a database you own.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should the table on competitor comparison landing pages include?\", \"a\": \"The table should hold the rows a buyer decides on, each side's answer in plain words, and a source link under every rival cell. Add the date each rival cell was checked. Drop rows where both products match, unless buyers expect to see them.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I learn which features to compare on competitor comparison landing pages?\", \"a\": \"Ask them. Send a five-question survey to recent customers and to deals you lost, asking which tools they looked at and which difference decided it. A training software company could borrow from <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/learning-and-development-questions'>learning and development survey questions</a> to hear how its buyers rank features. Emergent builds the survey from a prompt, with no response caps.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can competitor comparison landing pages name the rival brand they compare against?\", \"a\": \"Yes. The FTC's policy on comparative advertising encourages naming competitors, but requires clarity and, if necessary, disclosure to avoid deceiving the consumer. In practice, say what you compared and link the rival's own page for each claim. For anything beyond that, ask a lawyer.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I make competitor comparison landing pages work on a phone?\", \"a\": \"Keep two columns on a phone: your product and one rival, with the row label above each pair of answers. Pin the column names to the top of the screen as the reader scrolls. Put a third rival behind a switch at the top instead of a sideways scroll.\"}, {\"q\": \"Which rival should I build competitor comparison landing pages against first?\", \"a\": \"Start with the rival your lost deals name first, because that page answers a question your buyers already ask. Check that people search the two names together before you write. A game studio can ask players which titles they also play with <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/game-questions'>game survey questions</a>, then compare against the one named first.\"}, {\"q\": \"How often should competitor comparison landing pages be updated?\", \"a\": \"Recheck every rival cell on a fixed schedule, such as every 90 days, and again whenever a rival announces new pricing. Change the check date on the page each time. In an app Emergent builds, each check date sits in your own database, and the app can email the page owner when a cell passes its age.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should competitor comparison landing pages show the rival's prices?\", \"a\": \"Show a rival's price only when the rival publishes it, and link the public page with the date you read it. If the rival quotes prices on request, say that instead of guessing a number. A price you estimated is a claim you cannot back up.\"}, {\"q\": \"What do buyers want from competitor comparison landing pages?\", \"a\": \"Buyers on a comparison page already have a shortlist. They want the one difference that settles it, with proof they can open and check. To hear it from your own readers, send <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/audience-questions'>audience survey questions</a> to your newsletter list before you write the rows.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
