      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Newsletter Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a newsletter landing page?\", \"a\": \"A newsletter landing page is a standalone web page with one goal: getting a visitor to subscribe to a newsletter. It says what each issue covers and how often it arrives, then asks for an email address, with no menu or other offer competing for the click.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a newsletter landing page?\", \"a\": \"Describe the newsletter to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder'>AI landing page builder</a>: who it is for and what should happen after someone signs up. Emergent builds the page and a subscriber database you own, and you change any part by prompting again. The free tier covers building and publishing.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should I look for in newsletter landing page examples?\", \"a\": \"Look at what each page shows before the email field. The newsletter landing page examples worth copying put a sample of the writing on the page, such as recent headlines, and state the schedule in plain words. Then count the form fields and check whether a confirm step follows the signup, which a screenshot will not show you.\"}, {\"q\": \"When does a newsletter landing page template help?\", \"a\": \"It helps when the layout is what slows you down. A newsletter landing page template fixes the look, but the tags and the sync to your email tool still have to be built. The form here is shorter than on a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/lead-generation'>lead generation landing page</a>, sometimes only the email. Emergent builds the page and its subscriber table from one prompt, with no template to adapt.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a subscribe landing page ask for besides an email?\", \"a\": \"One question at most, and only if the answer changes what you send. A role or a choice of sections works on a subscribe landing page, because each answer can decide which issues a reader gets. Ask nothing you will not use. The app Emergent builds keeps every answer with the email in a database you own.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is a landing page for newsletter signups better than a signup box on my homepage?\", \"a\": \"Use both. A dedicated landing page for newsletter signups gives you one link to share in a podcast or a guest post, and nothing on it competes with the subscribe button. The homepage box catches visitors who are already on your site. Track the two as separate sources to see which one brings in readers.\"}, {\"q\": \"How long should a newsletter landing page be?\", \"a\": \"Short: one phone screen for the headline and the form, plus a sample of the writing. A <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/squeeze-page'>squeeze page</a> cuts everything except the headline and the form. For a newsletter, leave room near the form for a few recent headlines or an excerpt, since readers judge a newsletter by its writing.\"}, {\"q\": \"How does a confirm link work on a newsletter landing page?\", \"a\": \"The new signup waits as pending while an email with a link goes out; the address counts as a subscriber only once its owner clicks it. That keeps mistyped and typed-in fake addresses from counting. Use it if you care more about who reads than about the raw count, and send one reminder before you drop an unconfirmed signup.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should a newsletter landing page show the subscriber count?\", \"a\": \"Show it once the number helps, and leave it off until then. A count in the thousands tells a visitor that other people chose this newsletter; a count of 40 can say the opposite. An app built with Emergent can show the count live from the subscriber table, and the figure on the page stays current.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I track which links bring visitors to my newsletter landing page?\", \"a\": \"Add a source tag to every link you share, such as ?src=podcast, and save it with each signup. Compare confirmed signups by source after 2 weeks rather than raw clicks. The same tag works on a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/lead-capture'>lead capture form</a> elsewhere on your site, and every row in the table then carries where it came from.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
