       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"QR Code Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a QR code landing page?\", \"a\": \"A QR code landing page is the page someone reaches by scanning a QR code on a package or a poster. It carries one message that matches the printed piece and one action, such as a short form, sized for a phone screen.\"}, {\"q\": \"How to create a QR landing page?\", \"a\": \"Build the page first, then make the code from its final link. Describe the page and its offer in one prompt to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder'>AI landing page builder</a> and publish it. Give every printed piece its own tagged link, make a QR code from each, and scan a printed proof before the full run.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where can I create a free landing page for my QR code?\", \"a\": \"You can build and publish one on Emergent for free, since the free tier covers building and publishing. Describe the page and its form in a prompt, publish it, and turn its link into a code with a QR code generator. Each signup is stored in your own database.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are the best practices for a QR code landing page?\", \"a\": \"Treat it as a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/mobile'>mobile landing page</a> first, because every visitor arrives from a phone camera. Repeat the printed offer in the headline word for word, ask for one thing, and keep the form on one screen. Under the code on the print, add a short line that says what the scan opens, such as Rate your meal.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are some QR code landing page examples worth copying?\", \"a\": \"Good examples open on the exact thing the person was looking at when they scanned. A yard sign can open the listing with a showing request, and a museum label can open the notes for that one piece. A product manual can open setup steps next to a warranty registration form.\"}, {\"q\": \"Does a QR code landing page generator make the QR code too?\", \"a\": \"Not every one does, so treat the page and the code as two separate jobs. Make the page first, then paste its final link into any QR code generator to make the code itself. If a generator offers to host the page too, ask where your form entries will be stored before you print anything.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should a QR code landing page play a video?\", \"a\": \"Only when the video is what the scan promised, such as setup steps printed on a product box. Keep the clip short and start it muted. Put the button or form above it so a visitor can act without watching. When one clip carries the whole pitch, build a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/video'>video landing page</a> around it instead.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I track which flyer or poster a QR landing page scan came from?\", \"a\": \"Give each flyer or poster its own link with a tag, then make a separate QR code from each link. Google's Analytics help says to add utm parameters in order to identify the campaigns that refer traffic. A tag such as utm_source=lobby_poster then marks the visits from that poster. Settle the tag names before anything goes to print.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I change the landing page for a QR code after it is printed?\", \"a\": \"Yes, as long as the link itself stays the same. A static code has the destination URL placed directly into it, and that URL can't be modified, but the page at that URL can change whenever you edit it. A dynamic code holds a short URL that redirects, and its destination can be changed after the code is created. On Emergent, a change to the page is one more prompt.\"}, {\"q\": \"How long should the form be on a QR code landing page?\", \"a\": \"Keep it to three fields or fewer when the scan leads to a signup or a rating. If the next step needs more, split it into a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/multi-step'>multi step form</a> with one or two questions per screen. Forms built on Emergent have no response caps.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     }
    ]
